# clef, the assembler in wolf (wolffe-lang/clef, public; the org's own
# assembler track): GNU-as AT&T x86-64 source to ELF relocatable objects.
# 996a3ccd is as01's merge (clef#8): all 43 x86-64 census sources match
# GNU as 2.42 in section contents, relocation tuples and structural
# symbols, and the kernel's seventeen assembly objects per tier link to
# kernels byte-identical to the GNU-as baseline. tools/mkclef builds it
# static from this commit for the image (as02b); tests/mpx5-clef
# qualifies the package on PAX. Opt-in (R-as02-3 A): no image carries it
# unless asked (tools/mkdev --clef), and tools/build-kernel uses it only
# when WOLF_AS names it. b71b43f4 is as02c's merge (clef#10): the word
# ports `inw %dx, %ax` and `outw %ax, %dx` and `xorq`, each encoded as GNU
# as 2.42 encodes it, with pax's boot/io.S (eb6592de, px76's kernel/power
# and triple fault) pinned as its fixture, byte-identical to GNU as.
CLEF_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/clef
# px97 (2026-11-04): clef trunk 900bdf0a, 49 commits after b71b43f4: its own
# toolchain to wolf 0.2.36 / lupin 0.1.58, every integer condition, alias,
# shift, extension, multiply and divide width encoded, LOCK validated on
# writable memory forms, the directive aliases and fills GNU as 2.42 takes,
# and the compiler's instruction envelope witnessed (census forms).
CLEF_REV=900bdf0a8f8f447bcc1505ecad1f65a367105dcc
